1
00:00:49,125 --> 00:00:51,750
It's called a "gas weapon."

2
00:00:51,750 --> 00:00:55,333
The gas contains some of my spinal fluid.

3
00:00:55,333 --> 00:01:00,083
Breathing just a slight amount
makes Subjects of Ymir freeze up.

4
00:01:00,083 --> 00:01:04,208
They can't control their bodies
and lose consciousness.

5
00:01:04,208 --> 00:01:11,333
On my command, I send the Power of
the Titans to the coordinate via Paths.

6
00:01:13,375 --> 00:01:17,875
That's why the people
of that village obeyed my orders.

7
00:01:17,875 --> 00:01:21,417
It's not "that" village. It's Ragako.

8
00:01:21,417 --> 00:01:26,583
Don't forget the name of the village
you slaughtered, you bearded shit.

9
00:01:26,583 --> 00:01:29,833
Well, I didn't want to do it.

10
00:01:29,833 --> 00:01:34,458
But if I hadn't, and they found out
I was sided with Eldia,

11
00:01:34,458 --> 00:01:38,542
I couldn't have brought hope to this island.

12
00:01:38,542 --> 00:01:43,417
You know, I told you all this
when I landed on the island.

13
00:01:43,417 --> 00:01:46,167
Why do you keep asking?

14
00:01:46,167 --> 00:01:51,000
You don't have a shred of guilt
in you and it shows.

15
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:57,917
You may or may not want to save Eldia,
but those lives meant nothing to you.

16
00:01:57,917 --> 00:02:04,125
You can't have been popular.
You think you know everyone's feelings.

17
00:02:04,125 --> 00:02:06,542
I do know.

18
00:02:06,542 --> 00:02:09,417
And I was popular enough.

19
00:02:09,417 --> 00:02:15,375
Well, ain't that great? So?
When will Eren and I begin the test?

20
00:02:15,375 --> 00:02:19,458
It's not up to me. We're waiting for HQ.

21
00:02:19,458 --> 00:02:24,125
They may think they have
time to spare, but they don't.

22
00:02:24,125 --> 00:02:26,083
I'm with you there.

23
00:02:26,083 --> 00:02:27,625
Captain Levi!

24
00:02:29,333 --> 00:02:32,500
What? Are you serious?

25
00:04:02,958 --> 00:04:07,958
"Children of the Forest"

26
00:04:08,958 --> 00:04:10,583
What a big building!

27
00:04:10,583 --> 00:04:12,542
I've never seen anything like it!

28
00:04:12,542 --> 00:04:13,750
Me, either!

29
00:04:13,750 --> 00:04:16,042
It's yer lucky day, kids!

30
00:04:16,042 --> 00:04:18,292
Y'all fixin' to eat?

31
00:04:18,292 --> 00:04:19,458
Yeah!

32
00:04:19,458 --> 00:04:23,000
What's wrong, Mia? Got the jitters?

33
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:24,458
Um, no...

34
00:04:24,458 --> 00:04:26,375
You're so nervous, Mia!

35
00:04:26,375 --> 00:04:29,167
I know! What a total bumpkin!

36
00:04:29,167 --> 00:04:30,583
N-No!

37
00:04:30,583 --> 00:04:35,083
Kaya! Does a Marleyan captive really work here?

38
00:04:35,083 --> 00:04:39,958
It's true, so get a grip.
Soldiers use this place, too.

39
00:04:39,958 --> 00:04:43,542
It'll be good to know another Marleyan.

40
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:48,167
Mr. Braus! Thank you for coming!

41
00:04:48,167 --> 00:04:51,333
Thanks a bunch for the invite!

42
00:04:55,583 --> 00:04:59,625
Oh, my. You sure brought a crowd.

43
00:04:59,625 --> 00:05:04,708
Since it's on the house,
I brought the whole gang. Sorry.

44
00:05:04,708 --> 00:05:08,542
It's fine. Welcome, everyone. This way, please.

45
00:05:08,542 --> 00:05:10,542
I'm starving, dad!

46
00:05:10,542 --> 00:05:13,000
--You and me both!
--We skipped breakfast for this!

47
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:16,750
That's Nicolo, the Marleyan
who invited Mr. Braus.

48
00:05:16,750 --> 00:05:18,917
See if he can help you.

49
00:05:18,917 --> 00:05:23,458
Mr. Braus isn't a soldier,
so why was he invited?

50
00:05:23,458 --> 00:05:27,500
His daughter was the girl
soldier who saved me.

51
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:34,542
Nicolo was at her grave and wanted
to treat him to the food she loved.

52
00:05:34,542 --> 00:05:39,167
But, personally, I thought they were in love.

53
00:05:43,167 --> 00:05:44,792
Ben?

54
00:05:44,792 --> 00:05:47,125
What's wrong? Tummy ache?

55
00:05:47,125 --> 00:05:49,000
Uh, no!

56
00:05:52,875 --> 00:05:56,917
Delicious! I've never had anything this good!

57
00:05:59,292 --> 00:06:02,917
Just wait till you've had the main dish!

58
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,208
Nicolo, you've got guests.

59
00:06:07,208 --> 00:06:10,792
Huh?! Who is it now?!

60
00:06:10,792 --> 00:06:13,667
The Scouts.

61
00:06:13,667 --> 00:06:20,875
You guys? What, is it urgent?
My hands are full with some customers.

62
00:06:20,875 --> 00:06:24,125
Uh, you can get back to work if you want.

63
00:06:24,125 --> 00:06:28,333
It's just, we'd like to talk once you're done.

64
00:06:28,333 --> 00:06:31,208
Talk? About what?

65
00:06:31,208 --> 00:06:34,958
Oh, you know. Like any concerns you have.

66
00:06:34,958 --> 00:06:40,292
They're investigating our detainment.
We're hoping you can help.

67
00:06:40,292 --> 00:06:43,042
Yeah, all right.

68
00:06:44,625 --> 00:06:46,583
You can wait here.

69
00:06:46,583 --> 00:06:49,417
Oh? What a fancy room.

70
00:06:49,417 --> 00:06:52,292
I bet it's reserved for MPs.

71
00:06:52,292 --> 00:06:57,083
Huh? Is this the wine all the
soldiers are gossiping about?!

72
00:06:57,083 --> 00:07:00,208
They say only higher ranks can get it!

73
00:07:00,208 --> 00:07:03,500
Yeah? Aren't we high rank in the Scouts?

74
00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:08,125
Yup! We deserve a bit
of fun, too! A sip or two--

75
00:07:08,125 --> 00:07:09,625
Don't touch that!

76
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:16,125
Ch-Chill out, Nicolo.
We're just screwing around.

77
00:07:16,125 --> 00:07:18,625
No need to overreact.

78
00:07:19,750 --> 00:07:23,667
This good stuff would be wasted on Eldians!

79
00:07:23,667 --> 00:07:27,708
Nicolo, you're still saying stuff like that?

80
00:07:27,708 --> 00:07:31,000
The booze don't give a damn what race we are!

81
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:37,250
Don't touch me, Eldian. Just because
I've been nice doesn't make us pals.

82
00:07:37,250 --> 00:07:40,833
Have you forgotten what you are? You're just a--

83
00:07:40,833 --> 00:07:46,625
A filthy captive, huh?
That makes us even, Eldian.

84
00:07:50,542 --> 00:07:52,542
What's his problem?

85
00:07:52,542 --> 00:07:55,708
Dammit! Hell if I know.

86
00:08:01,583 --> 00:08:02,542
Go.

87
00:08:02,542 --> 00:08:05,083
Argh! My stomach hurts!

88
00:08:05,083 --> 00:08:06,375
You okay, Ben?

89
00:08:06,375 --> 00:08:08,458
Eat something bad?

90
00:08:08,458 --> 00:08:11,167
I think I need to use the restroom!

91
00:08:11,167 --> 00:08:14,333
I think I better go help my brother!

92
00:08:14,333 --> 00:08:15,958
Good luck.

93
00:08:24,500 --> 00:08:28,333
Hmm? The restroom is the other way.

94
00:08:28,333 --> 00:08:30,917
That's not why we're here, Nicolo.

95
00:08:30,917 --> 00:08:35,042
We came from Marley. We're Warrior candidates.

96
00:08:35,042 --> 00:08:36,125
What?!

97
00:08:36,125 --> 00:08:41,833
We think there will be a huge
offensive against the island soon.

98
00:08:41,833 --> 00:08:47,792
Until then, hang in there! And let any
of your Marleyan comrades know!

99
00:08:47,792 --> 00:08:52,667
H-Hold up! What are Warrior
candidates doing here?

100
00:08:52,667 --> 00:08:55,917
The island devils raided Liberio.

101
00:08:55,917 --> 00:09:01,583
We got aboard their airship
as it retreated and rode it here.

102
00:09:04,125 --> 00:09:08,250
Did you... kill anyone?

103
00:09:08,250 --> 00:09:12,000
A female... soldier?

104
00:09:12,917 --> 00:09:14,792
Yes, I did!

105
00:09:14,792 --> 00:09:16,292
--I've only killed a few, but our real
revenge has yet to begin!

106
00:09:16,292 --> 00:09:20,750
--Gabi, wait! Hey!
--I've only killed a few, but our real
revenge has yet to begin!

107
00:09:20,750 --> 00:09:22,458
--We won't let those spineless
devils get away with...

108
00:09:22,458 --> 00:09:24,458
--Gabi, stop!
--We won't let those spineless
devils get away with...

109
00:09:24,458 --> 00:09:27,625
--What?!
--So it was you...

110
00:09:27,625 --> 00:09:30,458
...who killed her?

111
00:09:30,458 --> 00:09:33,500
You're the one who killed Sasha?!

112
00:09:45,500 --> 00:09:47,500
Falco?!

113
00:09:47,500 --> 00:09:49,958
Hey, Falco!

114
00:09:49,958 --> 00:09:53,417
Are you okay, Falco?!

115
00:09:53,417 --> 00:09:57,125
--Falco! Falco! Get up! Wake up!
Hey! Say something, Falco!

116
00:09:57,125 --> 00:10:00,083
--Shit!
--Falco! Falco! Get up! Wake up!
Hey! Say something, Falco!

117
00:10:07,042 --> 00:10:11,083
Nicolo! What'd ya do to Ben and Mia?!

118
00:10:11,083 --> 00:10:17,792
She's the one who killed Sasha.
She took your daughter's life.

119
00:10:19,042 --> 00:10:23,917
Though she's just a kid,
she's a trained Marleyan soldier.

120
00:10:23,917 --> 00:10:28,875
She got aboard the airship leaving
Marley and shot your daughter.

121
00:10:28,875 --> 00:10:31,625
She shot Sasha.

122
00:10:31,625 --> 00:10:33,500
Daughter?

123
00:10:36,500 --> 00:10:39,292
Mr. Braus, here.

124
00:10:39,292 --> 00:10:44,500
If you can't kill her, I will.
Is that all right?

125
00:10:49,542 --> 00:10:52,958
Wh-What the--?! Come here, guys!

126
00:10:52,958 --> 00:10:55,333
Huh? What is it?

127
00:10:56,292 --> 00:10:58,500
The kid who shot Sasha!

128
00:10:58,500 --> 00:11:03,542
What's going on, Nicolo?
I heard she's on the run!

129
00:11:03,542 --> 00:11:05,667
What do you think you're doing?! Hey!

130
00:11:05,667 --> 00:11:11,208
Don't move! Get back!
I'm avenging Sasha! Stay put!

131
00:11:13,333 --> 00:11:15,125
Stop...

132
00:11:15,125 --> 00:11:17,042
Not Falco!

133
00:11:17,042 --> 00:11:22,000
What is this brat to you?!
He took the hit for you!

134
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:25,750
Do you care about him?!
I cared about someone, too!

135
00:11:25,750 --> 00:11:28,833
An Eldian! Spawn of the devil!

136
00:11:28,833 --> 00:11:33,333
One who loved my cooking
more than anyone!

137
00:11:33,333 --> 00:11:37,083
She saved me from this shitty-ass war!

138
00:11:37,083 --> 00:11:41,958
She taught me that I like
making people happy with food!

139
00:11:41,958 --> 00:11:48,583
Her name was Sasha Braus!
She's the girl you stole from me!

140
00:11:48,583 --> 00:11:55,250
People I cared about were killed, too!
They were shot by your Sasha Braus!

141
00:11:55,250 --> 00:11:58,708
That's why I got revenge!
She killed people first!

142
00:11:58,708 --> 00:12:02,375
Who gives a damn who killed first?!

143
00:12:02,375 --> 00:12:05,708
Open your eyes! You're a Marleyan soldier!

144
00:12:05,708 --> 00:12:11,292
That devil woman bewitched you!
Don't lose to the devils!

145
00:12:12,708 --> 00:12:16,667
Nicolo, hand me the knife.

146
00:12:20,750 --> 00:12:22,583
Come on.

147
00:12:42,750 --> 00:12:45,833
Don't do it, Mr. Braus.

148
00:12:45,833 --> 00:12:49,083
Please put down the knife.

149
00:12:50,167 --> 00:12:52,833
Sasha was a hunter.

150
00:12:52,833 --> 00:12:54,083
What?

151
00:12:54,083 --> 00:13:00,083
Even as a wee girl, she shot
varmints in the forest for us to eat.

152
00:13:00,083 --> 00:13:03,625
That was just our way of livin'.

153
00:13:03,625 --> 00:13:09,500
But I knew there'd come a day we'd
have to give up that style of life,

154
00:13:09,500 --> 00:13:12,958
so I sent Sasha away from the forest.

155
00:13:12,958 --> 00:13:15,667
She went into the world,

156
00:13:15,667 --> 00:13:22,917
became a soldier, shot people
far yonder, and got herself shot.

157
00:13:22,917 --> 00:13:26,750
In the end, though she left our forest,

158
00:13:26,750 --> 00:13:32,833
the world is a great, big forest where
everyone's fightin' for their life.

159
00:13:32,833 --> 00:13:38,625
I reckon Sasha died 'cuz she
wandered in the forest too long.

160
00:13:38,625 --> 00:13:43,250
We've gotta keep the
younguns out of the forest.

161
00:13:43,250 --> 00:13:49,292
Otherwise, ain't nothin' gonna
stop it from happenin' again.

162
00:13:49,292 --> 00:13:56,958
That's why it's up to us adults
to shoulder the sins of the past.

163
00:13:56,958 --> 00:14:00,583
Nicolo, let Ben go.

164
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:11,000
Good, Lisa. Slowly, now.

165
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:12,542
Right.

166
00:14:12,542 --> 00:14:13,792
Are you hurt?

167
00:14:13,792 --> 00:14:18,125
Mia... You okay?

168
00:14:18,125 --> 00:14:20,333
Do you really...

169
00:14:21,292 --> 00:14:23,625
...not hate me?

170
00:14:33,250 --> 00:14:34,167
--Kaya...
--How dare you kill her!

171
00:14:34,167 --> 00:14:36,000
--Kaya, stop!
--How dare you kill her!

172
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:39,833
You murderer! I thought you were a friend!

173
00:14:39,833 --> 00:14:42,667
Let's move you! C'mon!

174
00:14:56,708 --> 00:14:59,917
Now the food's gone cold.

175
00:15:01,583 --> 00:15:07,917
Hange, try to rinse out that kid's mouth.
Some wine got in it.

176
00:15:07,917 --> 00:15:09,208
Huh?

177
00:15:09,208 --> 00:15:13,167
Though... it's probably too late.

178
00:15:13,167 --> 00:15:16,875
What's in... the wine?

179
00:15:17,833 --> 00:15:21,958
I think... Zeke's spinal fluid.

180
00:15:21,958 --> 00:15:26,958
"Marleyan Cuisine: The famous red wine
of Southern Marley is often used
as a secret ingredient in their cuisine,
but is paired with meals as well."

181
00:15:30,833 --> 00:15:33,125
Zachary was killed?

182
00:15:33,125 --> 00:15:39,042
Yes. The Jaegerists effectively
control everything in the walls.

183
00:15:39,042 --> 00:15:46,750
We think it's all part of some plan Zeke
put together using Yelena and Eren.

184
00:15:46,750 --> 00:15:47,958
And?

185
00:15:47,958 --> 00:15:54,542
Soon, the Jaegerists may bring Eren to
see Zeke like they've been demanding.

186
00:15:54,542 --> 00:15:57,792
And Pyxis? Is he letting this happen?

187
00:15:57,792 --> 00:16:03,250
As you know, the commander
can be quite stubborn.

188
00:16:03,250 --> 00:16:09,417
He's gonna make sure Eren
gets eaten... by our own hands.

189
00:16:09,417 --> 00:16:11,417
That's right.

190
00:16:13,333 --> 00:16:19,542
I've saved Eren, over and over--
each time, more comrades dying.

191
00:16:19,542 --> 00:16:24,375
All because I believed
he was the hope of humanity.

192
00:16:24,375 --> 00:16:28,875
And look--this is where my beliefs got me.

193
00:16:28,875 --> 00:16:35,500
It's like some awful joke.
What the hell was the hope that we saw?

194
00:16:36,875 --> 00:16:40,792
All that struggle for a farce like this?

195
00:16:42,875 --> 00:16:46,292
Such bullshit. It's not even funny.

196
00:16:46,292 --> 00:16:50,000
There's another shithead
we should have eaten.

197
00:16:52,042 --> 00:16:56,542
What do you mean?!
Zeke's spinal fluid is in the wine?!

198
00:16:56,542 --> 00:17:00,167
I don't have proof, but...

199
00:17:00,167 --> 00:17:04,750
They packed the first scout fleet
to the brim with it--

200
00:17:04,750 --> 00:17:08,625
well more than any scouting mission needed.

201
00:17:08,625 --> 00:17:10,708
--Again.
--And...

202
00:17:10,708 --> 00:17:15,750
...around the time I secured
my job here as a chef,

203
00:17:15,750 --> 00:17:18,125
--I was told to serve it
to high-ranking officers.

204
00:17:18,125 --> 00:17:20,583
--One more time.
--I was told to serve it
to high-ranking officers.

205
00:17:20,583 --> 00:17:22,167
By who?!

206
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:26,125
Yelena.

207
00:17:26,125 --> 00:17:30,667
As far as I know, she's the only one in on it.

208
00:17:30,667 --> 00:17:33,792
Can't speak for the other volunteers.

209
00:17:33,792 --> 00:17:37,833
Th-This is the first time I've heard about it!

210
00:17:37,833 --> 00:17:43,667
It doesn't make sense! Don't Eldians
freeze up if they drink his spinal fluid?

211
00:17:43,667 --> 00:17:50,208
According to Zeke. Nobody witnessed it,
so there's no way to confirm it.

212
00:17:50,208 --> 00:17:56,500
But... the effectiveness of his
little lie has been enormous.

213
00:17:56,500 --> 00:18:02,500
Because nobody has frozen up,
no one is even aware they drank it.

214
00:18:02,500 --> 00:18:07,583
Yeah, but... You don't know for sure, right?

215
00:18:07,583 --> 00:18:10,000
Yeah, I can't prove it.

216
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:18,042
But Marleyans know how Zeke's
spinal fluid has been used in the past.

217
00:18:18,042 --> 00:18:23,625
About ten years ago,
we conquered a capital in just one night.

218
00:18:23,625 --> 00:18:27,042
Hundreds of Titans sprung up in the city.

219
00:18:28,708 --> 00:18:31,667
Unless that's what she's plotting,

220
00:18:31,667 --> 00:18:38,375
I don't know why she wants it served
to your military's top officers.

221
00:18:38,375 --> 00:18:44,458
So earlier, you grabbed the wine
away 'cuz you were protecting us?

222
00:18:44,458 --> 00:18:49,792
Who knows? I don't know what I'm doing.

223
00:18:49,792 --> 00:18:53,958
I came here to save the world
from island devils.

224
00:18:53,958 --> 00:18:58,667
Now that I've opened my mouth,
I'm sure my days are numbered.

225
00:18:58,667 --> 00:19:00,708
But, Mr. Braus...

226
00:19:00,708 --> 00:19:06,958
I don't think I can be like you,
but if this can serve as atonement...

227
00:19:07,875 --> 00:19:12,917
Killing a child? What's wrong with me?

228
00:19:16,750 --> 00:19:18,625
Nicolo...

229
00:19:21,875 --> 00:19:25,250
Why did you protect me?

230
00:19:25,250 --> 00:19:29,042
Because. I don't have a reason.

231
00:19:29,042 --> 00:19:36,875
I'm the one who killed your comrade.
I'm the one who bludgeoned the guard.

232
00:19:36,875 --> 00:19:41,500
Falco didn't do it. Kill me, not him.

233
00:19:42,500 --> 00:19:43,917
We won't kill you.

234
00:19:43,917 --> 00:19:46,792
But you want to, don't you?

235
00:19:46,792 --> 00:19:49,958
I don't want to kill you.

236
00:19:49,958 --> 00:19:54,000
Kill this, kill that...
It's all you think about.

237
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:56,292
Just like someone I know.

238
00:19:59,208 --> 00:20:00,542
Er--

239
00:20:05,042 --> 00:20:06,292
What's wrong?

240
00:20:06,292 --> 00:20:07,750
Commander Hange.

241
00:20:07,750 --> 00:20:09,583
Floch!

242
00:20:09,583 --> 00:20:11,667
I'm glad you're here.

243
00:20:11,667 --> 00:20:17,042
I imagine you know where Zeke's at.
We'll have you take us there.

244
00:20:17,042 --> 00:20:21,208
Wait. We have no intention of fighting you.

245
00:20:21,208 --> 00:20:27,292
We rejected your proposal.
We won't negotiate with the military.

246
00:20:27,292 --> 00:20:30,167
And why is that?

247
00:20:30,167 --> 00:20:32,042
It's Eren's decision.

248
00:20:32,042 --> 00:20:37,583
Pyxis would never leave the fate
of the island in our hands.

249
00:20:37,583 --> 00:20:40,292
I'm sure he's frantically devising a plan

250
00:20:40,292 --> 00:20:45,292
to take the Founder from Eren
while we're on the move.

251
00:20:45,292 --> 00:20:47,542
You're imagining things.

252
00:20:47,542 --> 00:20:53,208
Or is that what your comrades
in the Garrison Regiment said?

253
00:20:53,208 --> 00:20:57,792
Does it look like I'm one of your
lackeys that'll answer you?

254
00:20:57,792 --> 00:21:04,667
I suggest you get moving
before I prove to you that I'm not.

255
00:21:04,667 --> 00:21:08,625
Shit. How'd they know we were here?

256
00:21:08,625 --> 00:21:13,417
Greiz? Did Yelena put you up to this?

257
00:21:13,417 --> 00:21:20,917
Nicolo, you're too obsessed with Eldians.
I knew this day would eventually come.

258
00:21:20,917 --> 00:21:24,375
I was right not to tell you how to reach them.

259
00:21:24,375 --> 00:21:30,000
Floch, listen! We don't have time
to be fighting among ourselves!

260
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:34,583
Wine with Zeke's spinal fluid
was spread through the military!

261
00:21:34,583 --> 00:21:38,000
Zeke fooled us all with this plan of his!

262
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:44,250
So what? It'll just make
the idiot MPs into bigger idiots.

263
00:21:44,250 --> 00:21:46,875
Can we go?

264
00:21:46,875 --> 00:21:50,083
I never said the MPs drank it!

265
00:21:50,083 --> 00:21:54,375
No way! You guys knew about the wine?!

266
00:21:58,208 --> 00:22:01,875
Use your inside voice, please.

267
00:22:07,125 --> 00:22:08,667
We're going ahead.

268
00:22:08,667 --> 00:22:09,792
Okay.

269
00:22:09,792 --> 00:22:14,667
That voice... Floch must've come.

270
00:22:14,667 --> 00:22:16,333
Yeah.

271
00:22:24,875 --> 00:22:29,458
I wanted... to talk with you guys.

272
00:24:03,333 --> 00:24:07,083
The Jaegerists capture Hange and the others.

273
00:24:07,083 --> 00:24:14,208
Staring intensely at Armin and Mikasa,
Eren says that he wants to talk.

274
00:24:14,208 --> 00:24:17,088
Next episode: "Savagery."
